# Shape reference for edge/.env — dummy values only, never the real thing.
# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored (root .gitignore); this file is not.
#
# These two are for `wrangler` itself (via dev.sh sourcing this file), to
# authenticate the CLI against your Cloudflare account — Workers AI has no
# local simulation, so wrangler needs real credentials even just to run
# `wrangler dev`.
#
# `wrangler dev` also auto-loads .env and surfaces every key in it as a
# Worker-local binding (visible as env.CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN / env.
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID in its startup binding table, values hidden), even
# though src/index.ts's Env interface never declares or reads them. Harmless
# today since nothing in the Worker touches those keys, but don't assume this
# file's contents stay CLI-only if the Env interface ever grows — check what
# it actually declares.
#
# Create at Cloudflare dashboard → your profile icon → API Tokens → Create
# Token → Custom token → permissions: Account / Workers AI / Read AND
# Account / Workers Scripts / Edit, scoped to your account.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=REPLACE_ME

# From the dashboard's account overview sidebar, or run `npx wrangler whoami`
# once CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN is set to see it printed.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=REPLACE_ME
